<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n20432" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hēnĭŏchi</span></b> ,
			ōrum, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡνίοχοι</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a people of Asiatic Sarmatia</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 6, 4,
				4, § 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 6, 42</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Thyest. 1048</span></i>.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> Derivv. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hēnĭŏchus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the Heniochi</i>, <i>Heniochian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rates,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					P. 4, 10, 26</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Hē-nĭŏchĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., the same: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">montes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					6, 9, 10, § 26</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
